.TH DANBY-SPINNINGBALL 1
.SH NAME
danby-spinningball \- drag and Magnus lift on a spinning projectile
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/spinningball
.SH MODEL
x'=vx; y'=vy;
vx'=-D|v|vx-L omega vy;
vy'=-g-D|v|vy+L omega vx.
.PP
D gives quadratic aerodynamic drag and L omega rotates the velocity-dependent
Magnus acceleration perpendicular to motion.  Positive spin in this two-
dimensional convention produces upward lift on positive horizontal velocity.
.SH DISPLAY
The large spatial plot shows the actual height-versus-distance trajectory.
The adjacent telemetry plot shows speed against time.  Integration stops at a
linearly interpolated ground crossing, so reported range is not quantized to a
whole timestep.
.SH CONTROLS
Tracks set launch speed and angle, drag, lift, spin, and gravity.  Any change
relaunches the ball.  Space pauses, period steps, r relaunches, and q exits.
.SH NUMERICS
The regression suite turns off drag and lift and verifies the exact vacuum
kinematic derivatives and launch-speed decomposition.
